Z||000000||nette||09-10-2001||12:24 PM||||Flushed the coolant system and filled it according to ogre's instructions.  Went smooth, without a hitch.  Now the temp gauge doesn't hardly register a temp, even after driving the car enough to get it up to operating temp.  The gauge only moves above 100 a teeny bit.  What's goin' on?<P>nette||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-10-2001||07:23 PM||||did you put the thermostat back in? Are you sure it's good? Are you sure it's all the way in the neck, and right end first??<P>The gauge may be off. You can chack it against the ECM sensor if you can get your hands on an ECM scanner. (The gauge and ECM use different sensors.)<P>You can also check it with a contact probe on a digital thermometer or with an IR thermometer. Just touch/point it at the thermostat neck.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
